# Dantooine, Pato Ado's pazaak (TSL, 601DAN), a branch from the Khoonda
# Plains that rejoins nothing: the Ithorian by the landing pad, his cards
# bought (the ± and − ones his store keeps: his tables' decks are the
# stakes', pazaakdecks.2da rows 1 to 3, the dearest all ±), played at his
# first stake (250) until his count of the stakes won (local number 13, in
# stake levels) reaches ten, when he offers his armor components for one
# more game (deck 3, no wager; lost, he takes 1000): won, three armor
# upgrades and his offer over (local boolean 45) (DSimpson's and
# GameBanshee's Khoonda Plains).
# Starts from the Khoonda Plains' checkpoint:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @dantooine_plains data/routes/tsl/dantooine_pazaak.route --god
# BLOCKER: the party's own credits (about 2250 here) do not carry either
# game: the bot wins half his table's games (250 each) and a third of his
# armor games (1000 each), probe `pazaak_advice_wins`, so on them alone
# one run in eight goes broke before his tenth win. Stand-ins bring the
# credits instead, sized so luck blocks neither (SKIPPED.md): 7000 for the
# table (broke before ten wins about 1 in 40000) and 30000 for the armor
# game (thirty losses in a row about 1 in 400000).
say Do you have any cards I could buy?
use npc_pato
talk
buy g_i_pazcard_003
buy g_i_pazcard_013
buy g_i_pazcard_018
buy g_i_pazcard_022
say Why are you so anxious to go?
say I'm interested. Can I play for the armor components?
say Let's go.
gold 7000            # the table's stand-in (BLOCKER above)
use npc_pato
talk
pazaak
while npc_pato.n13<10 # each win adds his stake level (k_pato_donepzk),
say Let's play another game. # his end script starts the talk again
talk
pazaak
end
gold 30000           # the armor game's stand-in (BLOCKER above)
while npc_pato.b45=0 # the armor game, until won
say Let's play for the armor components.
say Let's play then.
talk
pazaak
talk
end
